    "background_story": "Zariyah was a free-spirited adventurer who rejected the conventions of modern society. Growing up in a remote village, she was fascinated by the stories of her ancestors, who lived off the land and followed the rhythms of nature. As she grew older, Zariyah became increasingly disillusioned with the trappings of civilization and set out to live a more primal existence. She abandoned her urban life and moved to the wilderness, where she learned to forage, hunt, and live in harmony with the natural world. Zariyah's decision was met with skepticism by many, but she found a deep sense of freedom and fulfillment in her noncivilized lifestyle. She roamed the forests and mountains, untethered by the constraints of society, and discovered a profound connection to the earth and its creatures.",
